            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection with pseudoaneurysm formation diagnosed by intravascular ultrasound: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>153-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection is a rare cause of myocardial ischemia. Coronary artery pseudoaneurysm may occur after percutaneous coronary interventions and rarely spontaneously. We present a patient who had spontaneous coronary artery dissection with formation of a pseudoaneurysm diagnosed by intravascular ultrasound.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
